                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "630d09d4-0dcb-4884-99ad-4a4279bbe881",
                                "sense_id": "e41dc8ae-0edf-38f3-8c4f-194c20af5da5",
                                "text": "The latter bond of adherence was, however, the more slender; for, in the acts regulating the borders, we find repeated mention of \"Clannes having captaines and chieftaines, whom on they depend, oft-times against the willes of their landeslordes.\""
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "9eab1cb0-29e6-44bd-9ad8-a537bcb6c2ab",
                                "sense_id": "e41dc8ae-0edf-38f3-8c4f-194c20af5da5",
                                "text": "Whereupon, by reason also that Winter was come vpon them, and foule weather increased with fogs and mists that so couered the land, as without danger of perishing they could not approch it: Sir Humfrey Gilbert and M. Hays were compelled much against their willes to retyre homewards: And being 300. leagues on their way, were after by tempestuous weather separated the one from the other, the ninth of September last, since which time M. Hays with his Barke is safely arriued, but of Sir Humfrey as yet they heare no certaine newes."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "9510bb29-d906-48bb-a3d9-ee1426dca3b1",
                                "sense_id": "e41dc8ae-0edf-38f3-8c4f-194c20af5da5",
                                "text": "King Edmund, who hated nothing woorse than to linger his businesse, assembled his people, and marching forward toward his enimies, approched neere vnto them, & pitcht downe his tents not farre from his enimies campe, exhorting his people to remember their passed victories, and to doo their good willes, at length by one battell so to ouerthrow them, that they might make an end of the warre, and dispatch them cleerelie out of the realme."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
